           "The Portuguese captain who opened the sea route to India; portraits show a heavy beard and the cross of the Order of Christ.",
           "On the first European voyage round Africa to India, da Gama's crews fell sick on the East African coast. Historians of vitamin C note that the curative effect of citrus fruit was already known on this expedition. The voyage home was worse. By the time the fleet reached Malindi in January 1499 about half the crew had died and many of the rest had scurvy. There were not enough healthy men to sail three ships, so da Gama had the *Sao Rafael* scuttled. Of roughly 170 who left Lisbon, Jonathan Lamb counts 116 dead.",
           "The route to India was paid for in scurvy, and the cure was already in Portuguese hands.",
